# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository and the working tree.
#
# Rationale: the repo's .editorconfig and Biome both require `eol=lf`, but
# Windows checkouts with `core.autocrlf=true` smudge files to CRLF on checkout.
# That makes `biome format` (pnpm format:check) report a CRLF diff on virtually
# every file locally, even though every committed blob is already LF and CI
# (Linux) sees them as clean. This file makes Git store LF and check out LF on
# every platform, so the local format noise disappears for new clones.
#
# Existing Windows working trees keep CRLF until re-checkout / `git add
# --renormalize .`; we intentionally do NOT bulk-renormalize here because that
# would rewrite thousands of files and conflict with every in-flight branch.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary types: never normalize line endings.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.svg   text  eol=lf
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
